548
00:30:22,380 --> 00:30:25,020
One pretty vital or
important thing for us to

549
00:30:25,020 --> 00:30:28,260
know about is another
wave called the U-wave.

550
00:30:28,380 --> 00:30:31,260
As you can imagine, in
the alphabet, the letter U

551
00:30:31,260 --> 00:30:35,580
comes after T, so it's not
hard to see that it is another

552
00:30:35,580 --> 00:30:38,640
inflection in the ECG that
comes after the U-wave.

553
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:41,660
The U-wave itself
represents repolarization of

554
00:30:41,660 --> 00:30:44,340
Purkinje fibers and it's
always there in the ECG but

555
00:30:44,340 --> 00:30:46,280
it's usually so small
that we can't really tell.

556
00:30:46,540 --> 00:30:49,520
Now for this reason
again super high yield

557
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:52,020
for us to recognize
shallow T waves with

558
00:30:52,020 --> 00:30:54,980
a U wave is characteristic
of hypokalemia.

559
00:30:55,340 --> 00:30:58,140
A way to remember this
is substituting the

560
00:30:58,140 --> 00:31:02,320
O in hypokalemia with
U or hypokalemia.

561
00:31:02,830 --> 00:31:05,040
The reason why we care
about low electrolytes

562
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:08,320
like potassium is that,
as we mentioned before,

563
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:12,100
prolongation of the QT
interval, which if we

564
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:14,720
remember it to our
prior lectures, can

565
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:18,170
