579
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:56,340
So again, just
for hypercalcemia,

580
00:31:57,180 --> 00:31:59,460
QT interval shortening
is pretty much

581
00:31:59,460 --> 00:32:01,480
the hallmark of what
we're going to see.

582
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:05,040
So when it comes to
calcium, the more imminently

583
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:08,400
dangerous of the
calcaemias for the heart is

584
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:11,960
hypocalcemia. As we mentioned
before, in hypocalcemia

585
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:14,220
and in general,
following our general

586
00:32:14,220 --> 00:32:16,020
paradigm, when we have
a low concentration of

587
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:19,640
electrolytes, we're likely
to see QT interval changes,

588
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:22,140
