of the QT interval.

589
00:32:22,540 --> 00:32:25,340
Now, this may be
problematic because we all

590
00:32:25,340 --> 00:32:27,440
know that a prolonged
QT interval redisposes

591
00:32:27,440 --> 00:32:30,160
us to something. And
what is that condition?

592
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:32,540
Right, torsades de point.

593
00:32:33,460 --> 00:32:37,640
Hypocalcemia, hypokalemia,
and hypomagnesemia can

594
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:40,940
actually cause QT prolongation,
which can lead to torsades.

595
00:32:40,940 --> 00:32:43,880
This is pretty high yield
to know, specifically the

596
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:48,620
electrolytes. And it can
also help us remember the

597
00:32:48,620 --> 00:32:54,580
association between low
electrolyte, QT prolongation,

598
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:56,340
and torsades de point.

599
00:32:56,500 --> 00:32:59,550
So again, establishing
and grouping

600
00:32:59,550 --> 00:33:02,840
